name conceptnet-assertions
# One edge on every line, five fields parted by tabs, no header row. No documentation of the file is on this machine,
# so no column is given a name: the columns are told apart by their position in the row (1 .. 5), and the position is
# never recorded. The second, third and fourth fields are the edge, recorded in the row's own order, each as written:
#   /r/Antonym   /c/ab/агыруа/n   /c/ab/аҧсуа      is      [/c/ab/агыруа/n, /r/Antonym, /c/ab/аҧсуа]
# The fifth field is a JSON object that speaks of the edge, with names of its own (dataset, license, sources,
# surfaceText, surfaceStart, surfaceEnd, weight): everything in it is said of the edge itself. Its "sources" name who
# contributed the edge, under "contributor": each contributor is a witness of its own and attests the edge. An edge
# that names no contributor is attested by ConceptNet.
# Not recorded: the first field, the edge's own identifier (/a/[/r/Antonym/,/c/ab/агыруа/n/,/c/ab/аҧсуа/]), which
# writes the same three things again.
match assertions.csv
grammar table
columns 1 2 3 4 5

claims
subject in 3
predicate in 2
object in 4
json 5
witnesses sources contributor
